Z||000005||phillip||04-15-2000||10:41 PM|||| unless it's been modded in some way mid to late 70's corvettes only put out in the 200 horse (or less,my 74 is rated at 190hp, i think '75 were rated at 165hp) range. i love the car but unless i do some mods (only starting some exhaust work now) i know better than to jump bad with anyone.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||04-16-2000||09:25 AM||||Yep, those stock mid 70's to early 80's Vettes aren't much faster than the stock Camaros.<P>Back in my hayday when I had a built-up 68 SS 396 Chevelle, a 69 Stingray rolled up next to me at a stoplight and challenged me. The Vette had a mean idle lope and the distinctive deep thundering exhaust throb of a healthy 427 big block. I decined the race and I told him I knew what that L88 emblem on his hood meant. He just smiled.<P>I'm proud one of our little V6 Fieros whipped butt on a Vette, it's especially sweet because of the big mouth owner getting put into place.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||04-17-2000||08:36 AM||||Nice kill! Just try and pick on some one your own size.. like a C4 or a C5!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> even in the older cars, its MUCH more painful to the owner of the other car to get STOMPED by a V6 when he just dropped 30K in to a car...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   these people are SO weak... "my big block this, my small block that...or my GT or Cobra " BLAH, BLAH... my reply... i'm sure Shauns is too.. "oh really... well my PAID OFF Fiero will meet you at the light..."  do you have the stock valvebody in the tranny or do you have a shift kit? not that it matters i'm just curious. I had a 79 Stingray, Vermillion on Oyster.  Nice kill!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   VIVA LA FIERO! <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||1
